{
	"visualizations": {
		"viz_hdr_bg": {
			"type": "splunk.rectangle",
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.88)",
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.06)",
				"rx": 10
			}
		},
		"viz_hdr_title": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "## Admin Guide\n*Configuration reference, macros, data sources, and troubleshooting*",
				"fontColor": "#005073"
			}
		},
		"viz_overview": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "### Dashboard Overview\n\nThis app provides five executive dashboards for the **Florida Division of Emergency Management** statewide drill.\n\n---\n\n**Executive Dashboard** — `home_launchpad`\n> Top-level launchpad with domain scores — click any card to drill down\n\n**IT Health** — `it_health`\n> Network health, device health, compliance, open issues, syslog, config changes\n\n**Security** — `security`\n> Firewall, IDS/IPS, ISE, AD logons, VPN, DNS, email, web, XDR, PSIRT\n\n**User Experience** — `user_experience`\n> Client health, active clients, ThousandEyes, WAN latency\n\n**Building Resilience** — `building`\n> Occupancy, environmental sensors, power, cooling, compliance\n\n**Admin Guide** — `admin_guide`\n> This page"
			}
		},
		"viz_macros": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "### Index Macros\n\nAll queries use **index macros** instead of hardcoded index names. Each macro defaults to `index=*` (all indexes). To restrict queries to specific indexes, edit the macro definitions in:\n\n**Settings → Advanced Search → Search Macros** (filter by app `splunk-cisco-dashboards`)\n\n\n---\n\n**`index_catalyst`** — Catalyst Center (DNAC)\n> `cisco:dnac:client` · `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` · `cisco:dnac:devicehealth` · `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` · `cisco:dnac:compliance` · `cisco:dnac:issue` · `cisco:dnac:audit:logs` · `cisco:dnac:securityadvisory`\n\n**`index_firewall`** — ASA, FTD, eStreamer\n> `cisco:asa` · `cisco:ftd` · `cisco:sfw:estreamer`\n\n**`index_identity`** — Cisco ISE\n> `cisco:ise:syslog`\n\n**`index_windows`** — Windows / Active Directory\n> `XmlWinEventLog` · `ActiveDirectory` · `MSAD:NT6:DNS`\n\n**`index_network`** — IOS Syslog\n> `cisco:ios`\n\n**`index_meraki`** — Meraki Sensors and Uplinks\n> `meraki:sensorreadingshistory` · `meraki:devicesuplinkslossandlatency` · `meraki:audit`\n\n**`index_spaces`** — Cisco Spaces (Firehose API)\n> `cisco:spaces:firehose` (eventTypes: DEVICE_COUNT, CAMERA_COUNT, IOT_TELEMETRY, DEVICE_PRESENCE)\n\n**`index_security`** — XDR, Umbrella/SSE, ESA, WSA, SD-WAN UTD\n> `cisco:xdr:incidents` · `cisco:cloud_security:dns` · `cisco:cloud_security:firewall` · `cisco:esa:amp` · `cisco:esa:antispam` · `cisco:esa:content_scanner` · `cisco:wsa:squid` · `cisco:wsa:l4tm` · `cisco:sdwan:utd:logs`\n\n**`index_bms`** — Building Management System *(placeholder — not yet integrated)*\n> `bms:power` · `bms:hvac` · `bms:pdu`\n\n---\n\n**Example** — point Catalyst Center data at a dedicated index:\n```\n[index_catalyst]\ndefinition = index=cisco_dnac\n```"
			}
		},
		"viz_demo": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "### Demo Mode\n\nEvery dashboard has a **Demo Data** toggle in the top-right corner.\n\n- **On** (default) — if a query returns no real data, synthetic demo values are generated so visualizations are never empty\n- **Off** — only real data is shown; empty queries display `0`, `N/A`, or blank charts\n\nThe toggle sets the token `$demo_mode$` to `on` or `off`. Demo fallback data is produced by `| makeresults` blocks guarded by `| where \"$demo_mode$\"=\"on\"`.\n\n---\n\n**How it works in each query:**\n\n```\n1. Search real data `index_catalyst` sourcetype=\"cisco:dnac:client\" | stats ...\n2. Null guard | appendpipe [| where isnull(count) | eval count=0]\n3. Demo fallback | append [| makeresults | where \"$demo_mode$\"=\"on\" | eval count=42]\n4. Pick first result | head 1\n```\n\nReal data always wins because it appears first in the pipeline. Demo data only surfaces when the real search returned nothing **and** demo mode is on."
			}
		},
		"viz_datasources": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "### Required Data Sources\n\nEach technology below requires a Splunk add-on (TA) or app to collect data.\n\n---\n\n**Cisco Catalyst Center (DNAC)** — `TA_cisco_catalyst`\n> `cisco:dnac:client` · `clienthealth` · `devicehealth` · `networkhealth` · `compliance` · `issue` · `audit:logs` · `securityadvisory`\n\n**Cisco ASA / FTD Firewalls** — `Splunk_TA_cisco-asa`\n> `cisco:asa` · `cisco:ftd`\n\n**Cisco Secure Firewall (eStreamer)** — `TA-eStreamer`\n> `cisco:sfw:estreamer`\n\n**Cisco ISE** — Syslog\n> `cisco:ise:syslog`\n\n**Cisco Meraki** — `Splunk_TA_cisco_meraki`\n> `meraki:sensorreadingshistory` · `meraki:devicesuplinkslossandlatency` · `meraki:audit`\n\n**Cisco Spaces** — `Cisco Spaces Firehose Add-on`\n> `cisco:spaces:firehose` (eventTypes: DEVICE_COUNT, CAMERA_COUNT, IOT_TELEMETRY, DEVICE_PRESENCE)\n\n**Cisco XDR** — `Cisco XDR App`\n> `cisco:xdr:incidents` · `cisco:xdr:incidents-summary`\n\n**Cisco Umbrella / Secure Access (SSE)** — `cisco-cloud-security`\n> `cisco:cloud_security:dns` · `cisco:cloud_security:firewall`\n\n**Cisco ESA** — `Cisco ESA Add-on`\n> `cisco:esa:amp` · `cisco:esa:antispam` · `cisco:esa:content_scanner`\n\n**Cisco WSA** — `Cisco WSA Add-on`\n> `cisco:wsa:squid` · `cisco:wsa:l4tm`\n\n**Cisco SD-WAN** — `Cisco SD-WAN App`\n> `cisco:sdwan:utd:logs`\n\n**Cisco ThousandEyes** — `ta_cisco_thousandeyes`\n> Uses the `Cisco_ThousandEyes` data model via `| tstats`\n\n**Cisco IOS** — Syslog\n> `cisco:ios`\n\n**Microsoft Active Directory** — `Splunk Add-on for Windows`\n> `XmlWinEventLog` (EventCodes: 4624, 4625, 4672, 4740)\n\n**Building Management (BMS)** — *Not yet integrated*\n> `bms:power` · `bms:hvac` · `bms:pdu` *(placeholder sourcetypes)*"
			}
		},
		"viz_troubleshoot": {
			"type": "splunk.markdown",
			"options": {
				"markdown": "### Troubleshooting\n\n---\n\n**All KPIs show 0 or N/A**\n\n- Verify data is flowing: run `| tstats count where index=* by sourcetype` in Search\n- Check that index macros point to the correct indexes (see Index Macros above)\n- Confirm the required add-ons are installed and enabled\n\n---\n\n**Demo data appears even though real data exists**\n\n- Expand the time range — the default is Last 24 hours; data may be older\n- Confirm the sourcetype name matches exactly what the add-on produces\n\n---\n\n**Dashboard links are broken after renaming the app**\n\n- All internal links use `/app/splunk-cisco-dashboards/` — update drilldown URLs if the app folder is renamed\n\n---\n\n**Visualizations appear but charts are empty**\n\n- Turn Demo Data **On** temporarily to confirm the chart is wired correctly\n- Use **Open in search** from the data source editor to test the query directly\n\n---\n\n### Sourcetype-to-Macro Reference\n\nWhen onboarding new data sources, use this table to determine which index macro needs updating. Run the **Index Tuning** saved search (`Admin - Macro Index Tuning`) to discover which indexes your sourcetypes land in, then update the corresponding macro via **Settings > Advanced Search > Search Macros**.\n\n---\n\n| Macro | Sourcetypes | Technology |\n|---|---|---|\n| `index_catalyst` | `cisco:dnac:*` | Catalyst Center (DNAC) |\n| `index_firewall` | `cisco:asa`, `cisco:ftd`, `cisco:sfw:estreamer`, `cisco:estreamer:data`, `cisco:firepower:syslog` | ASA / FTD / Firepower |\n| `index_identity` | `cisco:ise:syslog` | Cisco ISE |\n| `index_windows` | `XmlWinEventLog`, `ActiveDirectory`, `MSAD:NT6:DNS` | Windows / Active Directory |\n| `index_network` | `cisco:ios` | IOS Syslog |\n| `index_security` | `cisco:xdr:*`, `cisco:cloud_security:*`, `cisco:esa:*`, `cisco:wsa:*`, `cisco:sdwan:utd:logs`, `ms:defender:*` | XDR / Umbrella / ESA / WSA / SD-WAN / Defender |\n| `index_meraki` | `meraki:*` | Meraki Dashboard |\n| `index_spaces` | `cisco:spaces:*` | Cisco Spaces |\n| `index_thousandeyes` | `cisco:thousandeyes:*` | ThousandEyes |\n| `index_bms` | `bms:*` | Building Management System |\n| `index_dhcp` | `DhcpSrvLog` | Windows DHCP Server |\n| `index_f5` | `f5:bigip:*` | F5 BIG-IP |\n\n---\n\n**How to update a macro:**\n\n1. Run: `| tstats count where sourcetype=\"<your_sourcetype>\" by index`\n2. Note the index name(s) returned\n3. Go to **Settings > Advanced Search > Search Macros**, find the macro, and set `definition = index IN (idx1, idx2)`\n4. Restart Splunk or use `| debug refresh` to reload"
			}
		},
